---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Header from '../components/Header.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
---

<Layout
  title="Prism Terms of Service | T-Time Media"
  description="The terms for using Prism, the personal companion for your care and your journey."
  ogPath="/prism-terms"
>
  <Header />

  <section>
    <div class="wrap">
      <h2>Prism</h2>
      <p class="page-title">Terms of Service</p>
      <div class="doc">
        <p class="fineprint">Prism, by T-Time Media LLC &middot; Last updated: October 5, 2026</p>
        <p>These terms are an agreement between you and T-Time Media LLC (&ldquo;we&rdquo;, &ldquo;us&rdquo;) about your use of Prism. By creating an account or using Prism, you agree to them. If you don&rsquo;t agree, please don&rsquo;t use Prism. Our <a href="/prism#privacy">Privacy Policy</a> explains how we handle your information and is part of these terms.</p>

        <h3>1. Prism is not medical advice</h3>
        <p>Prism is a personal record-keeping and reminder tool. It is not a medical device, and it does not provide medical advice, diagnosis, or treatment. Nothing in Prism, including medication names offered as shortcuts, is a recommendation. Always rely on a qualified healthcare professional for decisions about your health, and never delay or disregard professional advice because of something in Prism. In an emergency, call your local emergency number.</p>

        <h3>2. Reminders</h3>
        <p>Reminders depend on your phone, its settings, and its operating system, and they can be delayed, silenced, or missed. Prism is a convenience, not a guarantee: you remain responsible for taking medications and attending appointments as directed by your care team.</p>

        <h3>3. Who can use Prism</h3>
        <p>You must be at least 16 years old to use Prism. If you are under the age of majority where you live, you may use Prism only with the permission of a parent or guardian, who agrees to these terms for you.</p>

        <h3>4. Your account</h3>
        <p>Keep your password private and your email address current, since that is how you sign in and how we reach you. You are responsible for what happens under your account. Tell us at <a href="mailto:support@ttimemedia.org">support@ttimemedia.org</a> if you think someone else has accessed it. You can delete your account at any time in the app, under Data and export.</p>

        <h3>5. Your information belongs to you</h3>
        <p>You own everything you put in Prism. You give us permission to store, process, and display it only as needed to provide Prism to you, as described in the Privacy Policy. We do not sell your information or use it for advertising. You can export it or delete it whenever you like.</p>

        <h3>6. Using Prism fairly</h3>
        <p>Please don&rsquo;t:</p>
        <ul>
          <li>use Prism to break the law or to harm, harass, or impersonate anyone;</li>
          <li>try to access another person&rsquo;s account or data, or get around Prism&rsquo;s security;</li>
          <li>interfere with Prism or the services that run it, including by overloading them or sending automated requests;</li>
          <li>copy, reverse engineer, or resell Prism, except where the law allows it.</li>
        </ul>

        <h3>7. Changes and availability</h3>
        <p>Prism is currently in testing, and features may change, pause, or end. We work to keep Prism available and your data safe, but we can&rsquo;t promise it will always be available or free of errors. Keep your own export of anything you can&rsquo;t afford to lose. If we ever plan to shut Prism down, we will give you reasonable notice and a way to export your data.</p>

        <h3>8. Ending your use</h3>
        <p>You can stop using Prism and delete your account at any time. We may suspend or close an account that seriously or repeatedly breaks these terms, and will tell you why when we can.</p>

        <h3>9. Disclaimers</h3>
        <p>Prism is provided &ldquo;as is&rdquo; and &ldquo;as available&rdquo;. To the fullest extent the law allows, we disclaim all warranties, express or implied, including warranties of merchantability, fitness for a particular purpose, and non-infringement.</p>

        <h3>10. Limits on our liability</h3>
        <p>To the fullest extent the law allows, T-Time Media LLC is not liable for indirect, incidental, special, consequential, or punitive damages, or for lost data or missed reminders, arising from your use of Prism. Our total liability for any claim about Prism is limited to the greater of the amount you paid us for Prism in the twelve months before the claim, or US$50. Some places don&rsquo;t allow these limits, so they may not apply to you.</p>

        <h3>11. Apple</h3>
        <p>If you downloaded Prism from the App Store, Apple&rsquo;s terms for the App Store also apply. These terms are between you and T-Time Media LLC, not Apple, and Apple is not responsible for Prism or its content.</p>

        <h3>12. Changes to these terms</h3>
        <p>We may update these terms. If a change is meaningful, we will update the date above and let you know in the app or by email before it takes effect. Continuing to use Prism after that means you accept the new terms.</p>

        <h3>13. Contact</h3>
        <p>T-Time Media LLC &mdash; <a href="mailto:support@ttimemedia.org">support@ttimemedia.org</a></p>
      </div>
      <nav class="page-nav" aria-label="Prism">
        <a href="/prism">About Prism</a>
        <a href="/prism#support">Support</a>
        <a href="/prism#privacy">Privacy Policy</a>
      </nav>
    </div>
  </section>

  <Footer />
</Layout>
